# Reviewer probe: pg_stat_io / pg_stat_wal availability on the M5 fault host
# host: /Users/peter/.pgrx port 28818 (pgrx PG18), checkpoint 9364abb79

$ SELECT version();
PostgreSQL 18.3 (Homebrew) on aarch64-apple-darwin25.2.0

$ SELECT count(*) FROM pg_stat_io;
79

$ SELECT coalesce(sum(reads + writes + writebacks + extends + fsyncs), 0)::bigint FROM pg_stat_io;   -- exact pg_stat_io_total() query
113567203

$ SELECT wal_records::bigint, wal_bytes::bigint FROM pg_stat_wal;   -- exact pg_stat_wal_snapshot() query
359065291	407713486649

Both views and both exact probe queries succeed on this host.
The lanes nevertheless print 'pg_stat_io unavailable' / 'pg_stat_wal unavailable'
because assert_postconditions() was called with before=None, not because the
view or column is missing.
